{"from": "text:isaiah-56-7", "type": "related_to", "to": "passage:mt-21-13", "note": "Matthew 21:13 quotes Isaiah 56:7; biblical cross-reference. The Great Isaiah Scroll carries Isaiah 56 and attests the quotation as a manuscript."}
{"from": "text:isaiah-5-1-2", "type": "related_to", "to": "passage:mt-21-33", "note": "Matthew 21:33 draws its vineyard fittings (hedge, winepress, tower) from Isaiah 5:1-2, 5:5; biblical cross-reference."}
{"from": "text:1-maccabees-13-51", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-21-08-branches-cloaks-on-road", "note": "1 Maccabees 13:51 records Simon's entry into the Jerusalem citadel 'with praise and palm branches' - the closest Jewish literary parallel to a branch-strewn triumphal entry; biblical-era cross-reference, not independent evidence."}
{"from": "claim:mt-21-04-05-zechariah-9-9-quoted", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-greek-minor-prophets", "note": "Manuscript search: the 8HevXII gr Minor Prophets scroll from Nahal Hever identifies fragments of Zechariah but none in chapter 9 verse 9; Wadi Murabba'at's Hebrew Minor Prophets scroll (Mur88) is listed without specified contents, so no manuscript attests the quotation yet."}
