{"from": "text:mishnah-shekalim-1-6", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:mt-21-12-tables-overturned", "grade": "C", "note": "The same Mishnah passage has the money changers sitting at their tables in the Temple - the tables the verse says were overturned; it attests the tables' presence in the Temple commerce, not the overturning. Split from the bundled cleansing claim per the architect's bundled-claims ruling (2026-11-15). Redacted c. 200 CE, so it may not describe the practice of the 30s CE exactly."}
